          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"target_translation\":\"I love you.\",\"dimensions\":{\"T\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.99,\"reason\":\"This is a direct first-person avowal that presents Pierre's love for Hélène as true. Its later characterization as a lie concerns sincerity, not its clear truth-conditional avowal force.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Je vous aime\"},{\"block_id\":\"later_1\",\"quotation\":\"«Je vous aime», которое было ложь\"}]},\"P\":{\"score\":1,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.87,\"reason\":\"The words contain no explicit promise, but weakly ratify Pierre's already socially established position as Hélène's fiancé and husband-to-be. The engagement had effectively been declared before this expression; Hélène gives no separate verbal uptake to these particular words, though the subsequent marriage confirms uptake of the broader engagement.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Je vous aime\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Пьер молча держал руку своей невесты\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"— Je vous aime! — сказал он, вспомнив то, чтó нужно было говорить в этих случаях;\"}]},\"E\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.97,\"reason\":\"The expression is not represented as an involuntary affective discharge. Pierre deliberately recalls and supplies the conventional words expected in the situation, and is dissatisfied with how they sound.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"— Je vous aime! — сказал он, вспомнив то, чтó нужно было говорить в этих случаях; но слова эти прозвучали так бедно, что ему стало стыдно за себя.\"}]},\"O\":{\"score\":2,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.91,\"reason\":\"Beyond avowing love, the expression functions as compliance with a courtship formula: Pierre says what he believes convention requires at this stage of the socially orchestrated engagement. This scripted social performance is not fully captured by T, P, or E.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"«Что-то такое особенное говорят в этих случаях», думал он\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"— Je vous aime! — сказал он, вспомнив то, чтó нужно было говорить в этих случаях;\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"After Pierre and Hélène have been publicly treated and blessed as an engaged couple, they are left alone. Hélène kisses Pierre; he then deliberately utters the expected French declaration of love, which sounds inadequate to him.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"mixed\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"The target itself does not explicitly promise marriage or future conduct. At most, Pierre weakly ratifies the already established fiancé relationship and his expected role as Hélène's husband-to-be. No explicit response to these particular words is supplied, although the broader engagement has already been socially recognized and the supplied text reports that they marry a month and a half later. Evidence of actual affection is mixed: the scene represents attraction and Pierre's thought that he loves her, while his later reflection calls the declaration a lie and says he never loved her.\",\"recognised_work\":true,\"recognition_note\":\"I recognize the supplied passages as the Pierre–Hélène engagement episode from Leo Tolstoy's War and Peace.\",\"limitations\":\"The evidence strongly establishes the expression's avowal form and scripted social function, but Pierre's immediate self-understanding conflicts with his later retrospective judgment. The exact degree to which this formula independently ratifies the engagement, rather than merely accompanying an engagement already imposed and accepted through conduct, remains uncertain.\"}"
        }
